  "reply_text": "*One merge-blocking finding.*\n\n*CRITICAL — `src/guard.js:12`: `canEdit` checks READ instead of WRITE.*\nJavaScript evaluates `===` before `&`, so `share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` becomes `share.mask & true`—effectively checking bit 1 (READ). On unlocked documents, viewers can edit, while a WRITE-only share cannot.\n\n*Recommended fix:* use `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`. Add regression tests for unlocked READ-only and WRITE-only shares; the current editor test has both bits set and misses this.\n\nAll 6 existing tests pass; I separately reproduced both incorrect permission results. No other findings, and no files changed.",
